From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:38:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: qcom,msm8953-camss: add the VFE VBIF
 regions

Each MSM8953 VFE has a VBIF block that the vendor software programs
(vbif-regs and vbif-settings in the vendor msm8953-camera.dtsi).
Describe the two VBIF regions as optional trailing entries, like
vfe0_vbif on MSM8939, so existing device trees stay valid.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/1a2d06241fc807e36b1d2893ef5b5cd3098d5bf1
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8953-camss.yaml        | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8953-camss.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8953-camss.yaml
index 6d776b0ca711..21944750ee37 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8953-camss.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,msm8953-camss.yaml
@@ -170,9 +170,10 @@ properties:
 
   reg:
     minItems: 13
-    maxItems: 13
+    maxItems: 15
 
   reg-names:
+    minItems: 13
     items:
       - const: csi_clk_mux
       - const: csid0
@@ -187,6 +188,8 @@ properties:
       - const: ispif
       - const: vfe0
       - const: vfe1
+      - const: vfe0_vbif
+      - const: vfe1_vbif
 
   vdda-supply:
     description:
